| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $x$ | $7$ | $5$ | $3$ | $1$ | $-1$ | $-3$ | $-5$ |\n| $y$ | $$ | $$ | $$ | $$ | $$ | $$ | $$ |\n\n$$\n\n$$\n\nNow, we work out the $y$ values using $y=t.$ This gives\n\n| **$t$** | $-3$ | $-2$ | $-1$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $x$ | $7$ | $5$ | $3$ | $1$ | $-1$ | $-3$ | $-5$ |\n| $y$ | $-3$ | $-2$ | $-1$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ |\n\n$$\n\n$$\n\nPlotting these points, we obtain the following curve:\n\n![](images/ef/ef5f33b74b59b5a62fd8670a8feb6487b01a97aed4a44a098a576d10d891bd68.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179998 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179730 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "90a5c75b-e93d-5f09-a126-3d0cb5ede2d5" :knowledge-point/title "Writing a Factorial in an Equivalent Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5f928683-2206-515e-9154-238c2b97ff67" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(k+2)\\cdot k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257621} {:answer/id #uuid "771aae05-3e43-53e5-a66d-413cfd014971" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(k+2)\\cdot (k+1)!" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257834} {:answer/id #uuid "8401c7a8-8de7-538a-b715-56aeb8b85245" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "None of the listed" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257952} {:answer/id #uuid "a0f47d0b-3af1-5625-9eef-20a43b3c90a7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(k+2)\\cdot (k+1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186258194} {:answer/id #uuid "baf66338-ec48-5785-9b89-dee745803bf5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(k+2)\\cdot k!" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186258420}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "771aae05-3e43-53e5-a66d-413cfd014971" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(k+2)\\cdot (k+1)!" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257834} :answer-field/id #uuid "a0b168bd-c6b6-557b-94bf-969806cf924b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186259315}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "06937889-7753-54db-a2ad-60dda70867ce" :question/math-academy-id "q-124142" :question/problem "Which of the following is equivalent to $(k+2)!$ for any $k\\ge 0?$" :question/worked-solution "Using the definition of factorial, we have \n\n$$\n(k+2)!=(k+2)\\cdot (k+1)\\cdot k\\cdot \\,⋯\\,\\cdot 2\\cdot 1.\n$$\n\nNow, applying the factorial definition to all but the first factor, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(k+2)! & =(k+2)\\cdot \\overset{(k+1)!}{\\overset{⏞}{(k+1)\\cdot k\\cdot \\,⋯\\,\\cdot 2\\cdot 1}} \\\\  & =(k+2)\\cdot (k+1)!\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186259682 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186083335 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "8d084334-b89a-5a33-9373-086018cdfbc3" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating the Factorial of Zero"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "639bcea5-e2bf-5810-bd1d-be75cc7c83f1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "25" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257658} {:answer/id #uuid "b3e498dc-6116-583e-9426-bf9c965b7848" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "120" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186258344} {:answer/id #uuid "f2acdf55-5a3c-5fa6-a227-9905caee424d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "125" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186258896} {:answer/id #uuid "f3cce177-3888-5e25-b5bb-13548db279fe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "119" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186258911} {:answer/id #uuid "feaa5d9d-3191-5d57-9370-7daa98ad5