w and $2$nd column. \nSince $B$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix, it does not have the $3$rd row. \n\nTherefore, $B$ does not have the entry ${b}_{32}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186398270 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100989 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ecd07ea0-767d-55f0-a61c-da49dd320f89" :knowledge-point/title "Finding an Entry of a Square Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "98fbdf20-acf5-515a-bfa3-137c87680aa9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398272} {:answer/id #uuid "f57e452e-091d-53c6-b537-9d8de53dadd9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398273} {:answer/id #uuid "b0722739-e1d1-5718-ba55-c85b60d5ab23" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No such entry" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398274} {:answer/id #uuid "3a635fff-4506-56cc-99fc-a57d55714d75" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398275} {:answer/id #uuid "b97ac68a-e69b-5baf-9965-278548d78bf7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398276}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3a635fff-4506-56cc-99fc-a57d55714d75" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398275} :answer-field/id #uuid "3e8d8b4e-4a07-54ab-a806-9ff391023612" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398271}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "5aee8772-02f1-5e96-b1e0-f67b0c259d43" :question/math-academy-id "q-125593" :question/problem "Find the entry ${r}_{43}$ of the matrix $R$, where \n\n$$\nR=[\\begin{aligned}-5 & 2 & \\sqrt{3} & 4 \\\\ -3 & 0 & -4 & 5 \\\\ 5 & -2 & 8 & -1 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 1 & \\sqrt{2}\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The entry ${r}_{43}$ lies at the intersection of the $4$th row and $3$rd column. Therefore, ${r}_{43}=1.$\n\n$$\nE=[\\begin{aligned}-5 & 2 & \\sqrt{3} & 4 \\\\ -3 & 0 & -4 & 5 \\\\ 5 & -2 & 8 & -1 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 1 & \\sqrt{2}\\end{aligned}]\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186259831 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064245 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "abe88143-989a-5967-bb08-16804e31d948" :knowledge-point/title "Using Integration by Parts to Compute an Indefinite Integral Containing an Exponential Expression"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "109d035c-6ffc-56c3-8581-53bca2233532" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{x{e}^{2x+5}}{4}+\\frac{{e}^{2x+5}}{2}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256935} {:answer/id #uuid "209845fa-bfdf-5169-8a21-91e5d6fa04ab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x{e}^{2x+5}}{4}-\\frac{{e}^{2x+5}}{4}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257046} {:answer/id #uuid "5be69881-f41a-506d-a346-ccfa892bacb0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{(x+7){e}^{2x+5}}{4}-\\frac{x{e}^{2x+5}}{4}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257582} {:answer/id #uuid "6a4a072e-05a9-58e4-83e0-911e978158f4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{(x+7){e}^{2x+5}}{2}-\\frac{{e}^{2x+5}}{4}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257721} {:answer/id #uuid "a0da683e-5345-5b81-9094-abd5ff0ec151" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{(x+7){e}^{2x+5}}{4}+\\frac{{e}^{2x+5}}{2}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186258191}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6a4a072e-05a9-58e4-83e0-911e978158f4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{(x+7){e}^{2x+5}}{2}-\\frac{{e}^{2x+5}}{4}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257721} :answer-field/id #uuid "b284ab05-c542-58e4-99b1-8ce31da489d2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186259344}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "b258b659-45f7-5842-b37a-ee530a2eb1b6" :question/math-academy-id "q-12560" :question/problem "Calculate the integral $\\int (x+7){e}^{2x+5}\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "To solve this integral, we use the by-parts formula, given by\n\n$$\n\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x=uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nWe need to express $\\int (x+7){e}^{2x+5}\\,\\text{d}x$ as $\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x.$ Therefore, we set\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=x+7\\, & ⟹\\,{u}^{′}=1 \\\\ {v}^{′}={e}^{2x+5}\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\frac{{e}^{2x+5}}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe substitute the above into the integration by parts formula, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x & =uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int (x+7)\\cdot {e}^{2x+5}\\,\\text{d}x & =(x+7)\\cdot \\frac{{e}^{2x+5}}{2}-\\int \\frac{{e}^{2x+5}}{2}\\cdot 1\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we calculate the integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int (x+7){e}^{2x+5}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{(x+7){e}^{2x+5}}{2}-\\frac{1}{2}\\int {e}^{2x+5}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{(x+7){e}^{2x+5}}{2}-\\frac{{e}^{2x+5}}{4}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186400198 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100990 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "1cc70bda-40cf-5860-9a47-25f290c71041" :knowledge-point/title "Describing an Entry of a Matrix in Index Notation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "83bdeed3-df37-5030-9210-4fd26c862b5d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{y}_{31}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186400200} {:answer/id #uuid "5071b299-4f24-5216-a03b-d3bb38f10c37" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{y}_{41}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186400201} {:answer/id #uuid "6c05e69c-1e2c-58a5-8d1d-ec8b55b911ab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{y}_{32}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186400202} {:answer/id #uuid "7d163472-1ec4-5e60-97dc-1403c415123e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{y}_{42}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186400203} {:answer/id #uuid "214dd131-7e3a-56a7-b7fd-be2f662d3fd3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{y}_{43}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186400204}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7d163472-1ec4-5e60-97dc-1403c415123e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{y}_{42}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186400203} :answer-field/id #uuid "93e2aeb3-64f5-5d7d-b868-6bf0abe7eba8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186400199}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "a14b13fa-47dd-5e1a-8086-20e6009f70ea" :question/math-academy-id "q-125611" :question/problem "Consider the highlighted entry of the matrix $Y$ given below. Describe it in terms of ${y}_{ij}.$\n\n$$\nY=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ -4 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 7\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The entry lies at the intersection of the $4$th row and $2$nd column. Hence, we have ${y}_{42}=7.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186387636 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087788 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ffddeaa7-a247-54b0-af4b-a29d9bbeee6a" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Maclaurin Expansion of a Sum of Functions Using Standard Maclaurin Expansions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "47c72431-b1e8-5942-9dde-529f439c5c1b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{1+{x}^{2}}+\\frac{1}{1+x}=2-x+2{x}^{2}-3{x}^{3}+⋯" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387638} {:answer/id #uuid "bb783217-56db-5600-a8df-b25391ebe6d1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{1+{x}^{2}}+\\frac{1}{1+x}=2-x-{x}^{3}+4{x}^{4}+⋯" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387639} {:answer/id #uuid "ef160337-ca61-546d-8189-8c5edd646927" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{1+{x}^{2}}+\\frac{1}{1+x}=2-x-{x}^{3}+2{x}^{4}+⋯" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387640} {:answer/id #uuid "f78cf437-8e73-5ca0-86ef-c78c893a58df" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{1+{x}^{2}}+\\frac{1}{1+x}=2-x-3{x}^{3}+4{x}^{4}+⋯" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387641} {:answer/id #uuid "4d956603-8434-5007-913e-d969f1db3884" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{1+{x}^{2}}+\\frac{1}{1+x}=2-x+3{x}^{2}-4{x}^{3}+⋯" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387642}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ef160337-ca61-546d-8189-8c5edd646927" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{1+{x}^{2}}+\\frac{1}{1+x}=2-x-{x}^{3}+2{x}^{4}+⋯" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387640} :answer-field/id #uuid "383cb569-d021-5751-9947-210d48031c1f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387637}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "67a0d004-5494-5134-92a1-e9cce26797b4" :question/math-academy-id "q-125901" :question/problem "Find the first four non-zero terms of the Maclaurin expansion of $\\frac{1}{1+{x}^{2}}+\\frac{1}{1+x}.$" :question/worked-solution "The Maclaurin series for $\\frac{1}{1-x}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{1-x} & =1+x+{x}^{2}+{x}^{3}+{x}^{4}+⋯.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nReplacing $x$ with $-{x}^{2},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{1+{x}^{2}} & =1+(-{x}^{2})+{(-{x}^{2})}^{2}+{(-{x}^{2})}^{3}+⋯ \\\\  & =1-{x}^{2}+{x}^{4}-{x}^{6}+⋯.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSimilarly, replacing $x$ with $-x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{1+x} & =1+(-x)+(-x)^{2}+(-x)^{3}+(-x)^{4}+⋯ \\\\  & =1-x+{x}^{2}-{x}^{3}+{x}^{4}-⋯.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAdding the expansions for $\\frac{1}{1+{x}^{2}}$ and $\\frac{1}{1+x},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{1+{x}^{2}}+\\frac{1}{1+x} & =(1-{x}^{2}+{x}^{4}-{x}^{6}+⋯)+(1-x+{x}^{2}-{x}^{3}+{x}^{4}-⋯) \\\\  & =(1+1)+(-x)+(-1+1){x}^{2}+(-{x}^{3})+(1+1){x}^{4}+⋯ \\\\  & =2-x-{x}^{3}+2{x}^{4}+⋯.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186387643 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087789 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b839f19a-161c-5cb4-bc08-990f09afb900" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Maclaurin Expansion of a Logarithmic Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "46119b7e-db5d-5859-869c-4dfa02c4d11d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1+3{x}^{2})=3{x}^{2}-\\frac{9}{2}\\,{x}^{4}+9{x}^{6}-⋯" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387645} {:answer/id #uuid "50ec0bba-9f3e-5da1-9b72-0409f2cc5730" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1+3{x}^{2})=3{x}^{2}-\\frac{3}{2}\\,{x}^{4}+3{x}^{6}-⋯" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387646} {:answer/id #uuid "a34d6f1c-4ff1-5763-9d87-da27291ad35e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1+3{x}^{2})=-{x}^{2}+3{x}^{4}-9{x}^{6}+⋯" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387647} {:answer/id #uuid "a57274d6-bd9e-5bc0-ab24-b9d8e408fb52" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1+3{x}^{2})=-3{x}^{2}+\\frac{3}{2}\\,{x}^{4}+9{x}^{6}+⋯" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387648} {:answer/id #uuid "24f1d5e1-63d7-57b1-b641-e6546f03f818" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1+3{x}^{2})={x}^{2}-\\frac{9}{2}\\,{x}^{4}-3{x}^{6}-⋯" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387649}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "46119b7e-db5d-5859-869c-4dfa02c4d11d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1+3{x}^{2})=3{x}^{2}-\\frac{9}{2}\\,{x}^{4}+9{x}^{6}-⋯" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387645} :answer-field/id #uuid "606cd081-7f36-5393-8926-17e3abf81d50" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387644}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "a1ecfe56-a815-5a27-b4a2-19bbceb3f5f5" :question/math-academy-id "q-125912" :question/problem "Find the first three non-zero terms of the Maclaurin expansion of $\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1+3{x}^{2}).$" :question/worked-solution "The Maclaurin series for $\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1+x)$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1+x)=x-\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{2}+\\frac{1}{3}{x}^{3}-⋯.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nReplacing $x$ with $3{x}^{2},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1+3{x}^{2}) & =(3{x}^{2})-\\frac{1}{2}{(3{x}^{2})}^{2}+\\frac{1}{3}{(3{x}^{2})}^{3}-⋯ \\\\  & =3{x}^{2}-\\frac{9}{2}\\,{x}^{4}+9{x}^{6}-⋯.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
